1. [READ] Retrieve a list of tech companies from the provided source. | out company_list | api Tech Companies / List Companies
2. [PROCESS] For each company in $step1.company_list, extract relevant news articles. | out article_list | api News Aggregator / Get Articles | args {"companies": $step1.company_list}
3. [PROCESS] Analyze the sentiment of each article using a sentiment analysis tool. | out sentiment_analysis_results | api Sentiment Analysis / Analyze Text | args {"articles": $step2.article_list}
4. [PROCESS] Fetch the current stock prices for each company. | out stock_prices | api Stock Market / Get Prices | args {"companies": $step1.company_list}
5. [PROCESS] Combine sentiment analysis results with stock prices for each company. | out combined_data | api Data Integration / Merge Data | args {"sentiment": $step3.sentiment_analysis_results, "prices": $step4.stock_prices}
6. [PROCESS] Identify the top movers based on sentiment and price changes. | out top_movers | api Data Processing / Filter Data | args {"data": $step5.combined_data, "criteria": "sentiment AND price_change"}
7. [PROCESS] Save the daily summary report of the top movers into a spreadsheet. | out spreadsheet_content | api Spreadsheet / Update Sheet | args {"sheetName": "Top Movers", "data": $step7.top_movers}
8. [WRITE] Send the daily summary report via email. | out email_status | api MailRecipe / Send Email | args {"to": "$user.email", "subject": "Daily Top Movers Report", "body": "Please find the attached spreadsheet with today's top movers."}

1. [LOCAL] Start by defining the upcoming business trip destinations. | out destinations
2. [READ] For each destination, search for flight statuses using the provided flight numbers. | out flight_statuses | api Flight Status / Get Flight Status | args { "flightNumbers": "$destinations" }
3. [PROCESS] Convert the currency of the reported ticket prices to the user's home currency. | out ticket_prices_in_home_currency | api Currency Exchange Rates / convertCurrency | args { "amount": "$flight_statuses.ticketPrice", "from": "$flight_statuses.currency", "to": "$user.homeCurrency" }
4. [LOCAL] Check the current weather at the destination cities. | out weather_conditions | api Weather Forecast / Get Current Weather | args { "cities": "$destinations" }
5. [LOCAL] Compile a summary of flight statuses, ticket prices, and weather conditions. | out summary | api Report Generator / Create Summary | args { "flights": "$flight_statuses", "prices": "$ticket_prices_in_home_currency", "weather": "$weather_conditions" }
6. [WRITE] Send a summary push notification to the user's phone. | out notification_status | api Push Notification Service / Send Notification | args { "message": "$summary", "deviceToken": "$user.phoneToken" }

1. [LOCAL] Define the specific city for monitoring major public events. | out monitored_city
2. [READ] Retrieve a list of upcoming major public events in $monitored_city. | out event_list | api Event Calendar / Get Events | args {"city": "$monitored_city"}
3. [PROCESS] For each event in $event_list, extract the venue location. | out venue_locations | PROCESS {"events": $event_list, "operation": "extractVenueLocation"}
4. [READ] For each venue location, fetch the current weather forecast. | out weather_forecasts | PROCESS {"locations": $venue_locations, "operation": "fetchWeatherForecast"}
5. [PROCESS] Combine the event details, venue locations, and weather forecasts into a single structured format. | out combined_details | PROCESS {"events": $event_list, "venues": $venue_locations, "forecasts": $weather_forecasts, "operation": "combineDetails"}
6. [WRITE] Create a task in your project management tool with all the collected information. | out task_created | api Project Management Tool / Create Task | args {"details": $combined_details}

1. [LOCAL] Define list of favorite stocks and cryptocurrencies. | out favorite_assets
2. [READ] Set up monitoring for the defined favorite assets. | out monitoring_config | api Stock and Crypto Monitoring / Setup Alerts | args {"assets": $favorite_assets}
3. [LOCAL] Retrieve the latest price movements for the monitored assets. | out price_movements
4. [PROCESS] Filter out significant price movements. | out significant_movements
5. [READ] Scrape financial news articles related to the significant price movements. | out news_articles | api News Aggregator / Search Articles | args {"keywords": $significant_movements}
6. [LOCAL] Analyze the sentiment of each scraped article. | out sentiment_scores
7. [PROCESS] Summarize the sentiment analysis results. | out summary | api Sentiment Analysis / Analyze Text | args {"text": $sentiment_scores}
8. [LOCAL] Create an email message with the summary. | out email_summary
9. [WRITE] Send the email summary every morning. | out email_status | api Mailrecipe / Send Email | args {"to": "$user.email", "subject": "Daily Price Movement Summary", "body": "$step8.email_summary"}

1. [LOCAL] Define list of major tech news sites to monitor. | out news_sites
2. [LOCAL] Define company name to track. | out company_name
3. [READ] Fetch articles from each news site using their RSS feeds. | out articles | api News Aggregator / Fetch Articles | args {"sites": $news_sites}
4. [PROCESS] Filter articles to find those mentioning the company name. | out relevant_articles | api Article Filtering / Filter Articles | args {"keywords": $company_name}
5. [PROCESS] Summarize each relevant article. | out summaries | api Article Summarization / Generate Summaries | args {"articles": $relevant_articles}
6. [PROCESS] Analyze the sentiment of each summary. | out sentiments | api Sentiment Analysis / Analyze Text | args {"summaries": $summaries}
7. [PROCESS] Create a lead record in CRM with summary and sentiment score. | out lead_record | api CRM Integration / Add Lead | args {"summary": $summaries, "sentiment_score": $sentiments}
8. [WRITE] Update CRM with the new lead record. | out update_status | api CRM Integration / Update CRM | args {"lead": $lead_record}

1. [READ] Fetch the top trending tracks from a music chart. | out trending_tracks | api Music Chart API / Get Top Tracks
2. [PROCESS] For each track, search for the lyrics. | out lyrics_search_results | api Lyrics API / Search Lyrics | args { "tracks": $step1.trending_tracks }
3. [PROCESS] Generate a short analysis of the lyrical themes based on the retrieved lyrics. | out lyrical_analysis | api Lyrical Theme Analysis / Analyze Themes | args { "lyrics": $step3.lyrics_search_results }
4. [WRITE] Publish the summary as a post on your social media account. | out post_status | api Social Media API / Post Content | args { "content": $step4.lyrical_analysis, "platform": "social_media_platform" }

1. [LOCAL] Define list of movie titles as ["Movie1", "Movie2", "Movie3", "Movie4", "Movie5"]. | out movie_titles
2. [READ] For each movie title in $movie_titles, retrieve its IMDB rating. | out movie_ratings | api Movie Database / Get Movie Ratings | args { "titles": $movie_titles }
3. [PROCESS] Find the movie with the highest rating among the retrieved ratings. | out highest_rated_movie
4. [LOCAL] Set the calendar event for Friday at 7pm. | out calendar_event | api Calendar Management / Create Event | args { "title": "Team Movie Night", "start_time": "Friday 19:00", "end_time": "Friday 21:00" }
5. [LOCAL] Generate a short link for the trailer of the highest rated movie. | out trailer_link | api Video Hosting Service / Generate Short Link | args { "video_id": $highest_rated_movie.video_id }
6. [WRITE] Text all team members with the highest rated movie and the trailer link. | out text_message_status | api Messaging Service / Send Text Message | args { "recipients": $team_members, "message": "This week's movie night is 'Highest Rated Movie'. Check trailer here: $trailer_link" }

1. [LOCAL] Retrieve all donors' emails. | out donor_emails
2. [READ] For each donor's email, fetch their gift details including currency and amount. | out gift_details | api Gift Details / Fetch Gifts | args {"emails": $step1.donor_emails}
3. [PROCESS] Convert each gift amount to USD using exchange rates. | out converted_gifts | api Currency Exchange Rates / convertCurrency | args {"gifts": $step2.gift_details}
4. [PROCESS] Generate a PDF receipt for each donor with their converted gift information. | out receipt_pdf | api Receipt Generator / Create Receipt | args {"details": $step4.converted_gifts}
5. [WRITE] Store the generated PDF receipts in the cloud drive. | out storage_status | api Cloud Storage / Upload Files | args {"files": $step4.receipt_pdf}
6. [WRITE] Email the generated PDF receipt to the donor. | out email_status | api MailRecipe / Send Email | args {"to": "$donor_email", "subject": "Your Donation Receipt", "body": "Please find your donation receipt attached."}
7. [READ] Check for new donors who have made a gift this month. | out new_donors | api New Donors / Identify New Donors | args {"gifts": $step2.gift_details}
8. [WRITE] Add new donors to the newsletter list. | out newsletter_status | api Newsletter List / Add Donors | args {"emails": $step7.new_donors}

1. [LOCAL] Generate a campaign image using design software. | out campaign_image
2. [LOCAL] Create a short link for the donation page. | out short_link
3. [LOCAL] Generate a QR code for the donation page. | out qr_code
4. [LOCAL] Write a campaign post with the image, short link, and QR code. | out campaign_post
5. [WRITE] Email the campaign post to the supporter list. | out email_status | api Mailrecipe / Send Email | args {"to": "$user.supporter_list_emails", "subject": "Join Our Giving-Day Campaign", "body": "$step4.campaign_post"}
6. [WRITE] Text the volunteer list to share the campaign post. | out sms_status | api SMS Service / Send SMS | args {"to": "$user.volunteer_list_phone_numbers", "message": "$step4.campaign_post"}

1. [LOCAL] Set up a task to monitor news mentioning the cafe. | out task_id | api News Monitoring Task / Create Task | args {"entity": "our cafe", "frequency": "daily"}
2. [LOCAL] Score each news mention for positivity. | out scores | api News Sentiment Analysis / Analyze Text | args {"text": "$news_mention"}
3. [LOCAL] Identify and flag any negative mentions. | out flagged_mentions | PROCESS | args {"scores": $scores, "threshold": -0.5}
4. [LOCAL] Open a task for negative mentions. | out negative_task_id | api Task Management / Open Task | args {"description": "Negative mention found", "task_type": "monitoring", "status": "open", "details": "$flagged_mentions"}
5. [LOCAL] Collect all mentions for posting in staff chat. | out all_mentions | PROCESS | args {"mentions": $news_mention}
6. [LOCAL] Post all mentions in staff chat. | out chat_posted | api Chat System / Post Message | args {"message": "$all_mentions", "channel": "staff"}
7. [LOCAL] Select the most positive mention for a thank-you post. | out best_mention | PROCESS | args {"mentions": $news_mention}
8. [LOCAL] Prepare a thank-you post with the selected mention. | out thank_you_post | PROCESS | args {"mention": $best_mention}
9. [LOCAL] Publish the thank-you post weekly. | out published | PROCESS | args {"post": $thank_you_post}

1. [READ] Retrieve the list of performers and their songs for the open-mic night. | out performers_list | api Event Management / Get Performers List
2. [PROCESS] For each song in $step1.performers_list, look up the lyrics. | out lyrics_lookup_results | api Lyrics Lookup / Find Lyrics | args { "songList": $step1.performers_list }
3. [PROCESS] Flag songs with strongly negative or explicit tone based on the lyrics. | out flagged_songs | api Tone Analysis / Analyze Lyrics for Tone | args { "lyricsList": $step2.lyrics_lookup_results }
4. [LOCAL] Add the open-mic night event to the calendar. | out calendar_entry_added | api Calendar Management / Add Event | args { "eventName": "Open-Mic Night", "date": "Next Saturday" }
5. [PROCESS] Text each performer their assigned slot. | out texts_sent | api SMS Messaging / Send Texts | args { "performerList": $step1.performers_list, "slotInfo": "Your slot is confirmed." }
6. [LOCAL] Compile the running order including all songs, including flagged ones. | out running_order | api Event Management / Generate Running Order | args { "songsList": $step1.performers_list }
7. [WRITE] Post the running order in the volunteers' chat. | out chat_posted | api Chat Management / Post Message | args { "chatRoom": "Volunteers", "message": "$step6.running_order" }

1. [LOCAL] Prepare a list of 40 donated items with their short descriptions. | out item_list
2. [PROCESS] Generate illustrations for each item based on the provided descriptions. | out illustrations | api Illustration Generation / Create Illustrations | args { "items": $item_list }
3. [PROCESS] Compile the illustrations into a printable catalog. | out catalog_pdf | api Catalog Creation / Create Printable Catalog | args { "illustrations": $illustrations }
4. [LOCAL] Save the catalog PDF to the local drive. | out catalog_saved | api File Management / Upload File | args { "file_path": "local_drive/catalog.pdf" }
5. [LOCAL] Generate a short link for the saved catalog. | out catalog_link | api Link Generation / Create Short Link | args { "long_url": "file:///local_drive/catalog.pdf" }
6. [LOCAL] Draft a post announcing the auction. | out auction_announcement | api Content Creation / Write Post | args { "title": "Charity Auction Announced!", "content": "Join us for an exciting charity auction featuring 40 unique donated items!" }
7. [LOCAL] Send the auction announcement to the registered bidders. | out email_status | api MailRecipe / Send Email | args { "to": "$registered_bidders_emails", "subject": "Charity Auction Announcement", "body": "$auction_announcement" }
8. [LOCAL] Compose an email to the registered bidders with the catalog link. | out email_content | api Content Creation / Write Email | args { "subject": "Charity Auction Catalog", "body": "Please find attached the printable catalog for our upcoming charity auction. Enjoy browsing! \n\nCatalog Link: $catalog_link" }
9. [WRITE] Send the email to the registered bidders with the catalog link. | out email_status | api MailRecipe / Send Email | args { "to": "$registered_bidders_emails", "subject": "Charity Auction Catalog", "body": "$email_content" }

1. [READ] Identify the three clubs our fantasy league follows. | out club_ids | api Fantasy League / Get Club IDs
2. [READ] Retrieve the upcoming fixtures for the identified clubs. | out fixtures | api Match Schedule / Get Upcoming Fixtures | args {"clubs": $step1.club_ids}
3. [PROCESS] For each fixture, fetch the weather forecast for the match city. | out weather_forecast | api Weather Forecast / Get Forecast | args {"cities": $fixtures.match_cities}
4. [PROCESS] Flag games where the weather is expected to be heavy rain. | out flagged_games | api Game Weather Checker / Check Weather | args {"fixtures": $fixtures, "weather_forecast": $step3.weather_forecast}
5. [PROCESS] Generate a preview PDF combining the fixtures and weather information. | out pdf_preview | api PDF Creator / Create Preview PDF | args {"fixtures": $step2.fixtures, "weather": $step4.flagged_games}
6. [WRITE] Save the generated PDF preview to the user's drive. | out pdf_saved | api File Storage / Upload File | args {"file_path": "preview.pdf", "content": $step5.pdf_preview}
7. [WRITE] Post the preview link in the league chat. | out link_posted | api Chat System / Post Link | args {"chat_id": "$league.chat_id", "link": "file:///preview.pdf"}

1. [LOCAL] Get today's date to calculate tomorrow's forecast and sunrise. | out today_date
2. [READ] Retrieve the weather forecast for tomorrow. | out tomorrow_forecast | api Weather Forecast / Get Forecast | args {"date": "$today_date"}
3. [LOCAL] Determine if it is a hot and dry day based on the forecast. | out is_hot_and_dry
4. [LOCAL] Calculate the sunrise time for tomorrow. | out sunrise_time | api Sunrise Sunset / Calculate Sunrise | args {"date": "$today_date"}
5. [LOCAL] Set the watering slot one hour after sunrise for hot and dry days. | out watering_slot
6. [LOCAL] Add the watering slot to the garden calendar. | out calendar_update_status | api Garden Calendar / Add Event | args {"event": "$watering_slot", "calendar_id": "$garden_calendar_id"}
7. [LOCAL] Identify the volunteer on duty for the next shift. | out volunteer_on_duty
8. [LOCAL] Prepare a text message to be sent to the volunteer. | out volunteer_text_message | api Text Messaging / Prepare Message | args {"recipient": "$volunteer_on_duty.phone_number", "message": "Your watering slot is scheduled for $watering_slot."}
9. [LOCAL] Post a note in the garden chat about the new watering slot. | out chat_post_status | api Chat System / Post Note | args {"note": "Watering slot set for $watering_slot.", "chat_id": "$garden_chat_id"}
10. [LOCAL] Send the text message to the volunteer. | out text_send_status | api Text Messaging / Send Message | args {"sender": "$user.phone_number", "recipient": "$volunteer_on_duty.phone_number", "message": "$volunteer_text_message"}

1. [LOCAL] Define list of specific ingredients to track. | out ingredients_list
2. [READ] Retrieve daily news articles. | out news_articles | api News Aggregator / Get Articles
3. [PROCESS] Filter news articles for mentions of ingredients in $ingredients_list. | out relevant_news | api News Filtering / Filter Articles | args {"keywords": $ingredients_list}
4. [READ] Fetch latest market prices for ingredients in $ingredients_list. | out market_prices | api Market Data / Get Prices | args {"ingredients": $ingredients_list}
5. [PROCESS] Combine relevant news articles with their corresponding market prices. | out news_with_prices | api Data Merging / Merge News and Prices | args {"news": $relevant_news, "prices": $market_prices}
6. [LOCAL] Generate a weekly digest summary from $news_with_prices. | out weekly_digest | api Weekly Digest Generator / Create Summary | args {"data": $news_with_prices}
7. [WRITE] Send the weekly digest summary via email. | out email_status | api Mailrecipe / Send Email | args {"to": "$user.email", "subject": "Weekly Food Trends Digest", "body": "$weekly_digest"}

1. [LOCAL] Define the field of interest. | out field_of_interest
2. [READ] Retrieve the latest major scientific breakthroughs in the defined field. | out breakthroughs | api Latest Scientific Breakthroughs / Search | args {"field": "$step1.field_of_interest"}
3. [PROCESS] Filter out non-major breakthroughs. | out filtered_breakthroughs
4. [READ] For each breakthrough, fetch the primary research papers. | out papers | api Research Papers / Search | args {"breakthroughs": "$step3.filtered_breakthroughs"}
5. [PROCESS] Generate a concise summary of the findings from each paper. | out summaries | api Summarize Research Paper Findings / Generate Summary | args {"papers": "$step4.papers"}
6. [PROCESS] Format the summary for social media readability. | out formatted_summaries | api Format Text for Social Media / Format | args {"summaries": "$step5.summaries"}
7. [WRITE] Post a formatted thread about the discovery to the user's social media feed. | out post_status | api Social Media Platform / Post Content | args {"platform": "$user.social_media_platform", "content": "$step6.formatted_summaries"}

1. [READ] Retrieve a list of all open shipments. | out open_shipments | api Shipment Management / List Open Shipments
2. [PROCESS] For each shipment in $step1.open_shipments, check if it is past its promised delivery date. | out past_promised_date | api Shipment Management / Check Delivery Status | args {"shipmentIds": "$step1.open_shipments"}
3. [FILTER] Filter out shipments that are not past their promised date. | out filtered_shipments
4. [LOCAL] Determine the local business hours for the customers. | out local_hours
5. [LOCAL] Loop through each shipment in $step4.filtered_shipments and determine if it is past its promised date. | out flagged_shipments | api Shipment Management / Check Delivery Status | args {"shipmentIds": "$step4.filtered_shipments"}
6. [LOCAL] For each flagged shipment, text the customer with an update. | out text_status | api Customer Communication / Send Text Message | args {"customerIds": "$step6.flagged_shipments", "message": "Your shipment is delayed. We are working on it."}
7. [LOCAL] For each flagged shipment, open a support ticket. | out support_ticket_status | api Support Ticket System / Create Ticket | args {"shipmentId": "$step6.flagged_shipments", "status": "Delayed", "details": "Shipment is past promised date."}
8. [LOCAL] Summarize the delays and create a report. | out summary_report | api Report Generation / Create Report | args {"title": "Daily Delay Summary", "data": "$step7.support_ticket_status"}
9. [WRITE] Send the summary report to the sender. | out email_status | api MailRecipe / Send Email | args {"to": "$user.email", "subject": "Daily Delay Summary", "body": "$step8.summary_report"}

1. [LOCAL] Extract daily specials descriptions from the database. | out specials_descs
2. [PROCESS] For each special, extract nutrition facts using a nutrition API. | out nutrition_facts | api Nutrition Facts / Extract Nutrients | args { "description": "$step1.specials_descs" }
3. [PROCESS] Generate a photo for each special using a photo generation API. | out special_photos | api Image Generation / Create Photos | args { "descriptions": "$step1.specials_descs" }
4. [PROCESS] Build the specials menu page combining nutrition facts and photos. | out menu_page | api Web Page Builder / Construct Menu | args { "nutrition": "$step2.nutrition_facts", "photos": "$step3.special_photos" }
5. [WRITE] Upload the constructed menu page to cloud storage. | out upload_status | api Cloud Storage / Upload Files | args { "files": "$step4.menu_page", "bucket": "restaurant-specials" }
6. [LOCAL] Prepare the social media post content including the menu link. | out social_media_post | api Social Media Content Creator / Craft Post | args { "link": "https://cloud-storage-url/restaurant-specials/menu-page.html" }
7. [WRITE] Post the social media content. | out social_media_status | api Social Media / Post Content | args { "content": "$step6.social_media_post", "platforms": ["Facebook", "Instagram"] }
8. [LOCAL] Retrieve VIP list from CRM system. | out vip_list | api Customer Relationship Management / Retrieve List | args { "type": "VIP" }
9. [WRITE] Send text messages to VIP list with the specials menu link. | out sms_status | api SMS Messaging / Send Messages | args { "recipients": "$vip_list", "message": "Check out our weekly specials! Visit https://cloud-storage-url/restaurant-specials/menu-page.html" }

1. [LOCAL] Identify new interface strings added by developers. | out new_strings
2. [PROCESS] Check grammar of identified new strings. | out grammatically_correct_strings | api Grammar Checker / Check Grammar | args {"text": "$new_strings"}
3. [PROCESS] Translate each string into German, French, and Japanese. | out translated_strings | api Translation Service / Translate Text | args {"sourceText": "$grammatically_correct_strings", "targetLanguages": "de,fr,jp"}
4. [PROCESS] Ensure placeholders are not broken during translation. | out placeholder_preserved_translations | api Placeholder Preservation / Validate Translations | args {"translations": "$translated_strings", "placeholders": "true"}
5. [PROCESS] Flag translations that exceed the maximum allowed length for the UI. | out long_translations | api Translation Length Validator / Check Length | args {"translations": "$translated_strings", "maxLength": "100"}
6. [LOCAL] Save locale files to cloud storage. | out saved_files | api Cloud Storage / Upload Files | args {"files": "$translated_strings"}
7. [WRITE] Open a review task for translators. | out review_task_opened | api Task Management / Create Task | args {"taskType": "Translation Review", "description": "Review translations for new interface strings", "assignee": "Translator Team"}
8. [WRITE] Notify developers' chat about the new translations. | out chat_message_sent | api Chat System / Send Message | args {"message": "New interface strings have been added. Please review and translate them into German, French, and Japanese.", "channel": "$developer_chat_channel"}

1. [LOCAL] Create a new student account for each early-bird buyer. | out student_account
2. [LOCAL] Add each early-bird buyer to the course mailing list. | out mailing_list
3. [LOCAL] Generate and store login details for each early-bird buyer. | out login_details
4. [PROCESS] Create a short link to the course page. | out course_link | api Short URL Creation / Generate Short URL | args {"longUrl": "https://www.examplecoursepage.com"}
5. [LOCAL] Schedule live sessions on the calendar. | out calendar_event
6. [LOCAL] Announce the course launch on social media platforms. | out social_media_announcement | api Social Media Marketing / Post Announcement | args {"platforms": ["Facebook", "Instagram"], "message": "🎉 Exciting news! Our new online watercolor course is now live! 🚀 Join us for live sessions and start your artistic journey today! #watercolor #artclass #onlinelearning"}

1. [LOCAL] Read the item list. | out item_list
2. [PROCESS] Generate descriptions for each item in the item list. | out item_descriptions | api Item Description Generator / Create Descriptions | args { "items": $step1.item_list }
3. [PROCESS] Fix the grammar in the generated descriptions. | out fixed_descriptions | api Grammar Correction Service / Correct Text | args { "text": $step2.item_descriptions }
4. [LOCAL] Write the fixed descriptions to a markdown file. | out markdown_file
5. [LOCAL] Create a QR code linking to the markdown file. | out qr_code_image
6. [LOCAL] Create a flyer picture based on the markdown file. | out flyer_picture
7. [LOCAL] Upload the markdown file to a web server. | out web_link | api Web Hosting Service / Upload File | args { "file": "markdown_file.md" }
8. [LOCAL] Share the web link of the markdown file on social media. | out social_media_post | api Social Media Marketing / Share Link | args { "link": $step7.web_link, "platforms": ["Facebook", "Instagram", "Twitter"] }
9. [LOCAL] Send a text message to neighbors with the flyer picture. | out sms_message | api SMS Messaging Service / Send Message | args { "to": "$user.neighbor_phone_numbers", "message": "Check out my yard sale items at [web_link]. Here's a flyer.", "attachment": $step8.flyer_picture }

1. [READ] Find upcoming concerts in Montreal. | out concert_list | api Concerts / Search Concerts | args {"location": "Montreal", "dateRange": "tripDate"}
2. [PROCESS] For each concert in $step1.concert_list, check the weather for each show night. | out weather_info | api Weather Forecast / Get Weather | args {"city": "Montreal", "dates": "$step1.concert_list.showDates"}
3. [PROCESS] Convert ticket prices from Canadian dollars to euros for each concert. | out ticket_prices_eur | api Currency Exchange Rates / convertCurrency | args {"amount": "$concert.ticketPrice", "from": "CAD", "to": "EUR"}
4. [LOCAL] Select the two best shows based on ticket prices and reviews. | out selected_concerts | api Concert Reviews / Review Concerts | args {"concerts": $step3.concert_list}
5. [WRITE] Order tickets for the selected shows. | out order_status | api Ticket Booking / Book Tickets | args {"concerts": $step4.selected_concerts, "currency": "EUR"}
6. [LOCAL] Add the concert dates to your calendar. | out calendar_entry_added | api Calendar Management / Add Event | args {"events": $step5.order_status.eventDetails}
7. [WRITE] Email your friends the concert plan. | out email_status | api MailRecipe / Send Email | args {"to": "$friends.email", "subject": "Our Montreal Trip Concert Plan", "body": "We've booked the two best concerts and added them to our calendar. Check the attached link for more details."}

1. [LOCAL] Parse and extract GPS points from the birdwatching data. | out gps_points
2. [LOCAL] For each GPS point, use a mapping service to find the nearest place name. | out place_names | api Geocoding API / Reverse Geocode | args {"latlng": "$gps_points.latitude + ',' + gps_points.longitude"}
3. [LOCAL] Add the day's weather information to each GPS point. | out weather_info | api Weather API / Get Current Weather | args {"location": "$gps_points.place_name"}
4. [LOCAL] Clean up species names by removing duplicates and standardizing them. | out cleaned_species | api Data Cleaning Service / Dedup and Standardize | args {"data": "$gps_points.species_list"}
5. [LOCAL] Remove duplicate entries from the cleaned dataset. | out unique_entries | api Data Cleaning Service / Remove Duplicates | args {"data": "$cleaned_species"}
6. [LOCAL] Upload the cleaned dataset to cloud storage. | out upload_status | api Cloud Storage Service / Upload Data | args {"file": "$unique_entries.cleaned_data.csv", "bucket": "birdwatching-data"}
7. [LOCAL] Calculate and email the totals of sightings to the group. | out email_totals | api Email Service / Send Email | args {"to": "$user.email", "subject": "Birdwatching Count Totals", "body": "Total sightings: $unique_entries.total_sightings"}
8. [LOCAL] Generate a summary of the birdwatching count for social media posting. | out social_media_summary | api Social Media Service / Create Post | args {"content": "Birdwatching count summary: $unique_entries.total_sightings sightings across $unique_entries.unique_species species. Check our full dataset for more details."}
9. [LOCAL] Post the summary on social media. | out post_status | api Social Media Service / Post Content | args {"platform": "Twitter", "content": "$social_media_summary"}

